  "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\, & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${u}_{23}=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9=3.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
